# Cloudflare Pages edge redirects.
# Copied verbatim into apps/docs/out/ by Next.js's static-export step,
# then read by CF Pages at deploy time.
#
# The docs Next.js app routes everything under [lang]/, so the on-disk
# layout is /en/<page>/index.html and /zh/<page>/index.html. fumadocs
# is configured with `hideLocale: "default-locale"`, which means the
# sidebar and internal navigation emit prefix-free URLs (`/agents/`,
# `/assigning-issues/`, …) for the default-language (English) routes —
# but those paths don't exist on disk.
#
# At runtime we use CF Pages' rewrite mode (status 200) to map every
# unmatched apex path back into the /en/ tree without changing the
# user-visible URL. CF Pages serves existing files (out/en/**,
# out/zh/**, out/sitemap.xml, out/_next/**) directly without consulting
# this file, so the catch-all only fires for the missing-on-disk
# prefix-free routes.
#
# Order matters — first match wins. The bare `/` rule comes first
# because splats can match the empty string; we don't actually need it
# (the catch-all would handle `/` with an empty splat), but spelling
# it explicitly avoids one layer of redirect-debugging the next time
# this hits a CF behavior change.

/    /en/    200
/*   /en/:splat    200
